{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/829859-a-political-chronicle-and-how-not-to-mess-it-up","id":829859,"title":"A political chronicle and how not to mess it up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-14T13:38:11-08:00","id":829859,"title":"A political chronicle and how not to mess it up","content":"I've recently found myself in a new situation: Storytelling a group of players that has started as mortals and don't know literally nothing about the Requiem's setting. Therefore, I am looking for a pleasant and efficient way to introduce them to the basics without the need to info-dump them or creating the impression that every vampire in town is just waiting in line to explain his Covenant's worldview on things.<br /> <br /> To further complicate things, we've agreed upon a political-chronicle, with an inter-Covenant struggle as adriving force. The whole premise is that there were two warring factions - the Cronites and the Sanctified (with Carthians and Ordo largely in the crossfire) but no Invictus, that have showed up relatively recently (~15 years) as a Giovanni-style crime family (only sans the necromancy) and dived right in guns blazing. Now they have pronounced themselves peacekeepers of the city, with their own Prince and Sherriff. The shortage of numbers has forced the other Covenants to form uneasy alliances - Ordo+LS and Carthians+Cronites. As a consolation, the former were offered control over the unions and transportation, while the latter manage clubs, porn and prostitution. The Invictus saved drug dealing, protection rackets and some legit businesses for themselves. Until recently, the status quo worked out pretty well, but the Prince - called the Blood Baron - has disappeared and left his neonate childe to run the office, for which he is more than underqualified. That has caused some of the more ambitious elements in every Covenant to plot some power play and the full-scale hot war is about to begin any week now.<br /> <br /> So far the players are sticking to Invictus, but then again we are only three sessions in. I have a couple of questions for this most helpful community:<br /> - How to present the three-way conflict so that it doesn't become a bloody mess of subplots with players making random choices because they don't know what the hell happens around them? <br /> - What might be the reason for a Prince to leave his office in the hands of his underqualified childe? Where could he go? I have a couple of ideas, but I'd like to hear yours.<br /> - Are there any sourcebooks, adventures or other materials that deal with a detailed political conflict? Damnation City maybe?<br /> - Do you have any other advice I could use that applies specifically to this kind of scenarios?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T17:42:45-08:00","id":829934,"title":"","content":"For your second question, the prince may have had something important come up that he couldn't let any of the elders that actually were qualified to run his office know about, like a threat to a touchstone or a long term project nearing completion, the point is that it should be something where his Childe was only person he could trust and said trust was more important than his qualification to run the city.<br /> <br /> Also, damnation city is a great guide to kindred politics, so it should be useful for this.<br /> <br /> My last bit of advice is something I've heard from a few people on these forums. It's easier to run a political game if you A.) have a list of every major NPCs' motives and how to plan to accomplish their goals and B.) plot out what will happen if the PCs do nothing, based on the info from A, and then run the NPCs actions based on how the PCs either help or hinder their plans and how they change the outcome of events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:02:29-08:00","id":833432,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the important thing is to know what the important characters want. You don't even need that many, just the main goal for the leader of each faction and whoever it is the PCs usually deal with. Once you know those, you can extrapolate how these characters will react when their plans go wrong (or right) and what they'll do next. Once you know what each group wants, how they'll go about getting it should become fairly obvious to you, and it won't be too hard to keep it all straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T12:24:18-08:00","id":833442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/829859-a-political-chronicle-and-how-not-to-mess-it-up?p=833432#post833432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the important thing is to know what the important characters want. You don't even need that many, just the main goal for the leader of each faction and whoever it is the PCs usually deal with. Once you know those, you can extrapolate how these characters will react when their plans go wrong (or right) and what they'll do next. Once you know what each group wants, how they'll go about getting it should become fairly obvious to you, and it won't be too hard to keep it all straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>2nded. If you want to add in complexity, you can do it later with sub-characters having different goals (in slightly higher priority) than their main faction. Spin them up as needed, and pretend they were like that the whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T06:15:03-08:00","id":834982,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Woland</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/829859-a-political-chronicle-and-how-not-to-mess-it-up#post829859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking for a pleasant and efficient way to introduce them to the basics without the need to info-dump them or creating the impression that every vampire in town is just waiting in line to explain his Covenant's worldview on things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a very similar situation fairly recently when I started running my own chronicle. Three new vampires, entirely clueless about the entire supernatural existence thing, suddenly appearing in a city with a well established Kindred culture. And then I literally gave them a vampire that was just waiting in line to explain everything to them.<br /> See, the city has certain Rules and certain Provisions. Among the Provisions was an old Ordo Dracul line someone put in as part of an alliance with the Carthians, which said:<br /> &quot;The wisdom of the Ordo Dracul is available to all Kindred in the form of tutelage of the ways, rules, traditions, and lore to the new, the uninitiated, and the unruly.&quot;<br /> This was pretty much forgotten within the city, because embracing was done only when allowed by the governing powers, and was a pretty big deal, so most sires took it upon themselves to educate their would-be or recently embraced childe. It was never used, as there was never a situation that would warrant its use. The three PCs are literally the first childer without established sires in the city in half a century. Hell, without certain unique circumstances surrounding their appearance, they would have been killed on the spot because they were &quot;unpermitted&quot; to exist.<br /> So, the lawyer of the gang found this obscure rule, approached one of the Ordo, and asked them about it. To avoid losing face and status at Elysium, the Ordo member &quot;gladly&quot; embraced the opportunity to exercise a Provision of the covenant, and teach the three neonates some basic Kindred etiquette, city layout, etc.<br /> Securing this event was a session in itself, but to keep most of the information accessible to the players, and the relaying of it less boring, I ran the actual &quot;tutelage&quot; through online chat.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}